    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "C \u00b7 Agent fleets \u2014 why CPU autoscaling fails here",
      "collapsed": false,
      "id": 13,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Activity execution latency by type",
      "id": 14,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, activity_type) (rate(temporal_activity_execution_latency_seconds_bucket{namespace=~\"$namespace\", namespace!~\"temporal_system|system|_unknown_\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{activity_type}} p95"
        }
      ],
      "description": "How long each Activity type takes to execute, p95.\n\nThis is the number that sets how many slots a Worker needs. One slot sustains roughly 1/latency activities per second, so:\n\n  50ms activity   \u2192 ~20/sec per slot  \u2192 10 slots \u2248 200/sec\n  5s LLM call     \u2192 ~0.2/sec per slot \u2192 10 slots \u2248 2/sec\n\nA hundred-fold difference in required concurrency for the same throughput. That is why the agent Worker is configured with 50 slots against the order Worker's 10, and why a single default across both fleets is wrong for one of them.\n\nInvokeModel appearing here at seconds while ChargePayment sits at milliseconds is the whole argument for separate task queues.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line"
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Slot utilisation vs CPU \u2014 the autoscaling trap",
      "id": 15,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 24
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "1 - (sum(temporal_worker_task_slots_available{worker_type=\"ActivityWorker\", job=~\"$role\"}) / clamp_min(sum(max_over_time(temporal_worker_task_slots_available{worker_type=\"ActivityWorker\", job=~\"$role\"}[$__range:])), 1))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "slot utilisation (approx)"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "avg(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{name=~\".*worker.*\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "cpu cores per worker"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Slot utilisation beside CPU, to show that the two DISAGREE for an IO-bound fleet \u2014 which is the reason to autoscale on schedule-to-start rather than CPU.\n\nAn agent Worker spends nearly all its time blocked on a provider's HTTP response. It can sit at 100% slots busy \u2014 completely unable to accept another task \u2014 while showing a few percent CPU. A CPU-based autoscaler sees an idle fleet and never scales; the queue backs up and schedule-to-start climbs with nothing on a CPU chart to explain it.\n\nSLOT UTILISATION HERE IS AN APPROXIMATION and honest about it: the SDK exports slots AVAILABLE, not slots CONFIGURED, so the denominator is inferred from the high-water mark over the window. That is only correct if the fleet was idle at some point in it \u2014 on a permanently busy fleet this READS LOW. The authoritative figure is MAX_CONCURRENT_ACTIVITIES, which the app knows and the metric does not.\n\nThe CPU line needs cAdvisor and is absent on this stack by default. A missing line is the honest rendering; a fabricated zero would read as 'idle' and argue for exactly the wrong conclusion.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line"
          },
          "decimals": 3,
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
